# The stage0 compiler's checker. It reads the model's entities row by row,
# accepts the stage0 subset, and refuses anything else with a `Rejection` at the
# word concerned. A program is several modules, each starting with its module
# entity; they are checked one after another, and what one declares is seen by
# the modules after it as `<module>.<name>` (D-114). For each module:
#
# - checkModuleDeclarations reads every entity of the module. Types are
#   numbered for the whole program: the built-in types 1 to 11 (String, Int64,
#   ExitCode, Bool, Byte, Region, the standard errors together as 7 (a
#   standard error is only branched on or passed on), the host library's
#   handles and `Bytes`: ByteBuffer, process.Arguments, time.Deadline, Bytes),
#   then the records, enums, `list.List` and `map.Map` typeInstances, tables,
#   and operationTypes of each module in source order; string.Position, which
#   the driver declares in a module of its own before the program's, is 12
#   (D-115). Record fields and enum variants become members; every standard
#   library target the subset compiles (the `builtinTargets` table), every
#   operation, every record constructor, field reader, and `with`, every
#   variant constructor, every list and map member, and every table's `rowAt`
#   and `length` becomes a call target with its argument slots, types, and
#   passing modes, its result type, and what it raises. The module's names are
#   entered in maps seeded with the built-in names and every earlier module's
#   names, and published to the program's maps as `<module>.<name>` when the
#   module is declared. Each call, task, and region is tied to the operation
#   its `in` row names.
# - checkOperation reads one operation: its inputs, lets, labels, and regions,
#   the values its steps bind (`branch ifNext` items, `case` payloads), each of
#   its calls against the call's target, and each step in order.
#
# The subset: modules of constants (built-in types, literal values),
# records, enums with payloads, lists, maps with String keys, tables of records
# (cells are literals or variants without payload), operationTypes, and
# operations with copied, borrowed, and borrowedMutable inputs, one output (or
# none), an output owned by a region input, `raises none`, an enum of the
# program, or a standard library error, `maxRecursion` on recursive
# operations, and regions. A main takes no input, gives an ExitCode, and
# raises nothing; an `async true` operation is compiled like any other, and a
# task runs when it is started, as in an executable (D-37). Steps: `do`,
# `set`, `goto`, `branch if`, `branch ifError`, `branch ifNext` over a list,
# a map's keys, or a table in a forEach loop, `match` and `case` on an enum of
# the program, `return ok`, `return error`, `start <task> into none`, and
# `join`. A call names its target with `invokes`, or calls through a value of
# an operationType with `invokesReference`. Labels may be loops of any kind;
# `maxIterations` is kept so the emitted program traps where `refined run`
# would. A type held by value in a record or enum (or a list's item or a
# map's value) must be declared above the type holding it, so the C structs
# follow source order.
#
# What is checked: every row's predicate is one the subset reads, on an entity
# of the kind it belongs to; fixed payloads (`typeParameter none`, `async
# false` on an operationType, `cleanedBy none`, ...) are exactly those; types
# are known; literals fit their types; argument slots, types, and passing
# modes match the target; results and caught errors have the target's types;
# the values a call passes and a step names exist with the types they need;
# `set` changes only mutable lets; a let of an operationType names an
# operation of that signature; labels and calls a step names exist; a case's
# variant belongs to the matched enum; returns give the operation's output or
# error type; and each label's steps are together. The flow rules (`refined
# check`'s R5xx: values set before use, every block ending in a jump,
# exhaustive matches, ownership) and imports and exports are not repeated: run
# `refined check` on a program before compiling it with stage0.
#
# This module is generated from tools/subset.dsl by tools/build.py; it is
# ordinary SemanticScript and is checked as such.